  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Law, Public Policy, and Society AA-T Degree' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published August 5, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7678/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: Cal-GETC. Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT). Official Total Units: 60-62; this seed models the first-listed/recommended path = 15+16+15+15 = 61 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page; STAT C1000 at 4 units). Semester sums verified against the map's 15-16 / 15-16 / 15 / 15 headers. Major elective lists: List A (one course): ADMJ 300, ADMJ 320, ADMJ 322, ADMJ 480(H), BUS 340, BUS 345, SOC 319. List B (one course): COMM C1000, COMM 481(H), COMM 311, COMM 331 — COMM C1000 selected (COMM 311 used for List C). List C (one course): COMM 311, COMM 315, ENGL C1001, ENGL C1001H — COMM 311 selected. List D (one course, Area 2): ECON 310, PSYC 330, STAT C1000, STAT C1000H — STAT C1000 selected (4 units). List E (one course, Area 4): HIST C1001, HIST C1001H, HIST C1002, HIST C1002H, HIST 320, HIST 486(H), HIST 321, HIST 487(H), PHIL 310, POLS C1000, POLS C1000H — HIST C1001 selected. List F (TWO courses, 6 units total, from two DIFFERENT areas; courses must not have been used above): Area 1 Administration of Justice (ADMJ 300, ADMJ 302, ADMJ 304, ADMJ 320, ADMJ 480(H), ADMJ 322, ADMJ 323, ADMJ 340, ADMJ 349, SOC 318), Area 2 Business (BUS 340, BUS 345), Area 3 Economics (ECON C2002, ECON C2001), Area 4 Political Science (POLS 302, POLS 310, POLS 480(H), POLS 320), Area 5 Public Policy (GLST 301, GLST 302, SJS 300, SOC 301), Area 6 Diversity (ANTH 310, ANTH 481(H), COMM 325, ETHNS 300, ETHNS 320, ETHNS 330, ETHNS 341, ETHNS 350, ETHNS 360, GEOG 310, SOC 321, SOC 482(H), SOC 341), Area 7 College Success (HCD 310, INDIS 313). This path uses INDIS 313 (Sem 1, Area 7 — first-time college students select INDIS 313 per FYE note) and BUS 340 (Sem 2, Area 2 — a different area than Area 7, and not used above). Placement prereqs (documented, not in prereq arrays): students not placing directly in STAT C1000 take the STAT 10/STAT C1000 or STAT 10/PSYC 330 combo (PSYC 330 combo spring only); students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo. Advising notes: Area 5C lab component not required if a laboratory activity is included in 5A or 5B; the map also notes course overlap with the Legal Studies Certificate (List A BUS 345, List B COMM 311, List C ENGL C1001, Lists D/E/F one course each). Electives: any courses numbered 300-499 (see counselor). ADT requirements: all major courses with 'C' or better; 60 CSU-transferable units (12 within Los Rios); Cal-GETC Areas 1-6 with 'C' or better. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
